# Steel hub

This workspace is the **coordination vault**, not a product repo. Implement product
code in the spoke, not here.

Before implementing:

1. Read `index.md`, then `sprint/index.md` → whichever doc it names as current.
   **Never hardcode a sprint filename here** — sprints rotate and this rule outlives
   them. (This file pointed at an archived sprint for a month; that is the failure
   mode being designed out.)
2. Read `CLAUDE.md` at the vault root for the full agent contract — git conventions,
   the derived-not-transcribed rules, documentation policy. (Moved there from
   `ops/` on 2026-07-31; Claude Code loads it automatically, Cursor needs this line.)
3. If editing cross-repo facts, read `sync-registry.md` and `wiki/module-facts.md`.
   These cover the dormant geometry spokes only; course-lab has no cross-repo surface.
4. Implement in `C:/Users/rplap/OneDrive/Desktop/personal/<spoke>/` — paths are in
   `index.md` → Local paths.

Archived research (`archive/iste-narrative.md`, `archive/iste-alignment-findings.md`)
is historical. Do not treat it as canonical for code changes or agent instructions.

**No standing freeze.** The ISTE structural freeze expired with the event
(2026-07-01). If a freeze is ever in force again it will be stated in the current
sprint doc, which is the only place a deadline belongs.
